Z||000000||ChadMan||12-26-2001||08:58 AM||||My sister-in-law has a '93 Subaru Impreza with 122K miles on the original timing belt.  Do Subies bend their valves when their timing belts break?<P>Thanks in advance.<P>And in case anyone wondered, I still like my Miata, but I miss my Fiero every single day.  Especially now that it's wintertime and it never gets above 60 degrees in my car, and I can't see out the plastic rear window.<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||12-26-2001||10:10 AM||||Sorry, no info on whether the Subbies have interference engines or not, but most timing belts should be replaced every 60K.  Is it the original belt?  Might want to replace it anyway, if only to avoid being stranded somewhere.<P>The Miata doesn't have a powerful heater?  My father hasa Tracker convertable... the top is not lined at all.  Just one thin piece of canvas... and after about 15 minutes of driving its nice and toasty inside... and thats with temps in the 20's and snow everywhere here!  I guess its the price to pay for summertime top-down motoring!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Howard_Sacks||12-26-2001||02:36 PM||||Is it the sohc or dohc motor in it?  The 2.5L dohc motor had a TON of issues which is why subaru went back in 2000 to the sohc. I think I actually have heard of people bending valves at 70k on that motor.  Other than that, the flat fours are bullet-proof if maintained.<P>Check out <A HREF="http://www.i-Club.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.i-Club.com</A>,  and do a search in the discussion area or if you can't find anything post a question.  They're just as friendly as the fiero people in this forum, only they have all wheel drive ;-)<P><BR>Howard<P>with any luck, the link will work this time!<P>[This message has been edited by Howard_Sacks (edited 12-26-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Howard_Sacks (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||12-26-2001||03:13 PM||||Howard, you are the man!  My sis-in-law has the 1.8 SOHC, which according to i-club is NOT an interference engine.  That's great, because she's a waitress at Don Pablo's and isn't exactly rolling in $$$ and would wait until it broke to replace it anyway.<P>Fformula88, the Miata's heater sucks.  It heats up quickly, but the blower doesn't move a lot of air and the vents are undersized.||||reg||1
